    <string name="login_warning_privacy_title">Login privacy</string>
    <string name="login_warning_privacy">Sign in on Instagram\'s page inside the app. Your password and authentication code go directly to Instagram; the app does not collect them in native fields or send them to Python or a developer server. After you tap “Use this account”, the verified session cookies and browser identity are saved in encrypted app storage. Cookies can access your account. Logging out clears the saved session and WebView cookies.</string>
